To add a restart button to your Arduino code, you'll need to dedicate a digital pin to read the button's state and modify the code to reset the game variables when the button is pressed.

**Connection:**

1.  Choose an unused digital pin on your Arduino (e.g., pin 2 or 7).
2.  Connect one leg of the push button to this chosen digital pin.
3.  Connect the *other* leg of the push button to **GND** (Ground, which is the **minus**).

We will use the Arduino's internal pull-up resistor (`INPUT_PULLUP`) for the button pin. This means the pin will normally read HIGH (connected to positive voltage internally). When you press the button, it connects the pin to GND (minus), making the pin read LOW.

