1.  **`std::unique_ptr<Node> next;`**: Inside the `Node` struct, the `next` pointer is a `std::unique_ptr`. This means each `Node` exclusively owns the `Node` that follows it.
2.  **`std::unique_ptr<Node> head;`**: The `LinkedList` class holds a `std::unique_ptr` to the `head` node, signifying its ownership of the start of the list.
