## Model Railroad House Lighting Automation Project

This project uses an Arduino Nano, an external RTC (DS3231), and an OLED display to simulate daily house lighting patterns, including flickering TV effects, on an accelerated timescale for a model railroad layout.

### 1. Required Components

*   Arduino Nano
*   DS3231 RTC Module (or compatible)
*   0.96" I2C OLED Display (SSD1306 driver, 128x64)
*   LEDs (4x - e.g., white/yellow for rooms, blue/white for TVs)
*   Resistors (4x, e.g., 220Ω or 330Ω, suitable for your LEDs and 5V supply)
*   Tactile Pushbutton Switch (for night mode toggle)
*   10kΩ Resistor (optional, if not using internal pull-up for the button)
*   Breadboard
*   Jumper Wires
*   5V Power Supply for Arduino Nano

### 2. Circuit Wiring

1.  **Power:** Connect Arduino Nano 5V and GND pins to the breadboard power rails.
2.  **RTC Module:**
    *   Connect RTC VCC to 5V rail.
    *   Connect RTC GND to GND rail.
    *   Connect RTC SDA to Arduino A4 (SDA).
    *   Connect RTC SCL to Arduino A5 (SCL).
3.  **OLED Display:**
    *   Connect OLED VCC to 5V rail.
    *   Connect OLED GND to GND rail.
    *   Connect OLED SDA to Arduino A4 (SDA) (shared with RTC).
    *   Connect OLED SCL to Arduino A5 (SCL) (shared with RTC).
4.  **LEDs:**
    *   Connect Living Room Light LED anode (+) through a 220Ω resistor to Arduino D2.
    *   Connect Bedroom Light LED anode (+) through a 220Ω resistor to Arduino D3.
    *   Connect Living Room TV LED anode (+) through a 220Ω resistor to Arduino D5 (PWM capable).
    *   Connect Bedroom TV LED anode (+) through a 220Ω resistor to Arduino D6 (PWM capable).
    *   Connect all LED cathodes (-) to the GND rail.
5.  **Night Mode Button:**
    *   Connect one pin of the pushbutton to Arduino D4.
    *   Connect the other pin of the pushbutton to GND. (We will use the internal pull-up resistor on D4).

*(Alternative Button Wiring: Connect one pin to D4, the other pin to 5V, and add a 10kΩ pull-down resistor between D4 and GND. Adjust the code accordingly (`digitalRead(BUTTON_PIN) == HIGH` would mean pressed)).*

